      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-8636-1",
        "name": "USN-8636-1",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - x86 architecture;   - InfiniBand drivers;   - Media drivers;   - Network drivers;   - Mellanox network drivers;   - Texas Instruments network drivers;   - NVME drivers;   - File systems infrastructure;   - SMB network file system;   - IPv4 networking;   - Network traffic control;   - TCP network protocol;   - Locking primitives;   - Memory management;   - IPv6 networking;   - Multipath TCP;   - Netfilter;   - RxRPC session sockets;   - SCTP protocol;   - SMC sockets; (CVE-2026-31405, CVE-2026-31414, CVE-2026-31501, CVE-2026-31589, CVE-2026-31633, CVE-2026-31636, CVE-2026-31705, CVE-2026-43198, CVE-2026-43379, CVE-2026-43465, CVE-2026-43499, CVE-2026-46113, CVE-2026-46137, CVE-2026-46242, CVE-2026-46331, CVE-2026-52924, CVE-2026-52989, CVE-2026-53086, CVE-2026-53131, CVE-2026-53176, CVE-2026-53212, CVE-2026-53225, CVE-2026-53228, CVE-2026-53359)",
